  "configVersion": 0,
  "apple": {
    "version": "1.0",
    "copyright": "2026 LIBERTASIAN Inc.",
    "categories": ["REFERENCE", "EDUCATION"],
    "info": {
      "en-US": {
        "title": "LIBERTASIAN",
        "subtitle": "Philippine legal research",
        "description": "LIBERTASIAN is a Philippine legal research library for law students, bar reviewees, and practitioners.\n\n• Past Bar Exams — 97 sittings, 1,500+ questions from 1953–2024 with AI-generated ALAC answers for paid users.\n• Case Digests — Philippine Supreme Court cases with facts, issues, ruling, doctrine, and provenance, generated from authoritative sources only.\n• Codal Reader — Republic Acts, the 1987 Constitution, and the Rules of Court, organized by bar subject with cross-references.\n• AI Study Assistant — chat and Q&A grounded in what you are reading. Sourced answers only; the model abstains rather than fabricate.\n• Camera Scan-to-Digest — point your camera at a pleading or case printout and get a structured digest with citations back to the source.\n• Offline codal cache and cross-device sync between mobile and web.\n\nPrivate by default. Your uploads, scans, and notes stay scoped to your organization. Nothing you upload is ever used to train our models or shared without your explicit consent.\n\nLIBERTASIAN provides AI-powered legal research tools for informational purposes only. AI outputs are not legal advice and do not create an attorney-client relationship. Always consult a qualified Philippine lawyer for legal matters.",
        "keywords": [
          "Philippine law",
          "bar exam",
          "case digests",
          "codals",
          "Supreme Court",
          "jurisprudence",
          "RA",
          "RPC",
          "law school"
        ],
        "releaseNotes": "Initial release.\n\n• Browse Philippine Supreme Court case digests with provenance back to the source.\n• Read the 1987 Constitution, Rules of Court, and Republic Acts in the codal reader.\n• Drill 1,500+ past bar exam questions with AI-generated ALAC answers for paid users.\n• Scan a printout with your camera to generate a structured digest.\n• Offline codal cache and sync with libertasian.com on the web.",
